  "scope": "The statement-led critical-scheme derivation and the printed logarithmic-normal argument establish tangent dimensions(1,2,2,0), a smooth reduced locally miniversal bidisc and algebraic dimension1 for all sufficiently small deformations. Their differential/vector frames differ by the exact factors1/2 and2, their residue coefficients satisfy a_i=2h_i, and their coherent restriction maps are compared through the alternating pairing and conductor normalization. The new explicit interpolation inverse and Laurent-coefficient certificate check both old E13 computational steps by a different method after release. All nine proof items and every original displayed formula remain; the former E11 dependency is supplied by the actual local period matrix, cotangent connecting map and extension across the specified models. Public equation3.1/Proposition3.1 p6 and Proposition6.4 pp19--20 replace private source labels. Byte-identical code/output copies are delivered under code; the common Programs macro is retained without asserting new remote-file availability.",
